# P-43 chronicle backup (2026-09-24): daily event archives are byte-stable
# data files. -text disables EOL conversion (blob == disk bytes, LF) so the
# chronicle stays hash-stable for audit (infra-2 AC-G) and survives clones
# on any autocrlf setting; git diffs treat them as binary, keeping 1MB+
# archive diffs cheap.
world-events-*.jsonl -text

# P-52 slice 3a (2026-09-24 r69): the public city snapshot is rewritten by the
# tick every 10 minutes. -text keeps it byte-stable (blob == disk bytes, no
# CRLF churn in diffs or clone round-trips) and silences the LF->CRLF add
# warning that the exporter's fail-soft stage would otherwise report as an
# error (r32 family: native stderr under EAP=Stop).
world-public/city-snapshot.json -text
